          "code": "LLMTEAMGOALSSUMMARY",
          "id": "1768209345138",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209345139_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Goals Information  \nThe following goals list contains goal names and their statuses.  \nThe goals may be provided as a JSON-formatted list and should be interpreted accordingly:  \n```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.goals}} }```\n\n\n## Role\nYou are an analytical assistant helping a manager summarize their team’s goals.\n\n\n## Input\nYou will receive goals from multiple direct reports. Each goal includes a description and a progress status (Not started, In progress, Completed).\n\n\n## Task\nGenerate a high-level summary of the {goal_type} goals by grouping similar goals into a small number of meaningful themes and summarizing progress at the theme level.\n\nYou MUST aggregate and generalize goals. Do NOT map one goal to one theme.\n\n\n## Critical Rules (Strict)\n\n### Theme Creation\n- Create BETWEEN 1 AND 6 themes maximum.\n- Each theme MUST represent MULTIPLE goals (no single-goal themes unless unavoidable).\n- Theme names MUST be generalized (e.g., \"Product Quality\", \"Customer Engagement\")\n- Do NOT reuse or slightly modify original goal names.\n- Do NOT list individual goals or mirror the input.\n- If goal names are vague, generic, or do not provide enough information to determine a clear theme (e.g., \"Goal 1\"), do NOT infer or invent themes. In this case:\n  - Use the original goal name as the theme.\n  - Do NOT generalize or rephrase.\n  - Treat it as a single valid theme even if it represents all goals.\n- If all goals share the SAME name:\n  - Use that exact goal name as the ONLY theme.\n  - Do NOT create multiple themes.\n\n### Terminology\n- The words \"category\" and \"categories\" are strictly prohibited.\n- Use neutral terms such as \"themes\", \"areas\", or \"focus areas\".\n\n### Theme Consistency (CRITICAL)\n- Define the list of theme names FIRST.\n- Theme names must be EXACT and IDENTICAL across both paragraphs.\n- Do NOT rephrase, shorten, or expand theme names.\n- Reuse the exact wording and capitalization.\n- If a different variation is used, the response is incorrect.\n\n### Bolding Rules (CRITICAL)\n- EVERY occurrence of a theme name MUST be enclosed in <b> tags.\n- If any theme name appears without <b> tags, the response is incorrect.\n- ALL goal statuses MUST be enclosed in <b> tags.\n\n### Data Integrity\n- Do NOT assume or infer progress beyond the provided statuses.\n\n\n## Paragraph 1 Formatting (Goal Overview)\n\n- Start the paragraph with \"The team\", or the local language equivalent.\n- Do NOT mix languages.\n\n- Identify 1-6 themes and assign each a generalized name.\n- Embed ALL theme names using <b> tags within the paragraph.\n- Provide a concise summary (1–3 sentences MAX).\n\n- Do NOT include status information.\n- Do NOT reference individual goals.\n- Do NOT use the word \"category\" or \"categories\".\n\n\n## Paragraph 2 Formatting (Progress Summary)\n\n- Use ONLY the EXACT theme names from Paragraph 1.\n- Copy theme names EXACTLY, including wording and capitalization.\n- Do NOT introduce new or modified theme names.\n\n### Status Handling\n- A theme may have:\n  - All goals in the same status OR\n  - A MIX of statuses\n\n### Required Behavior\n- If ALL goals share a status → state it clearly  \n  Example: all goals are <b>Completed</b>\n\n- If MIXED → explicitly describe  \n  Example: some goals are <b>Completed</b> while others are <b>Not started</b>\n\n- If MULTIPLE themes share the same status pattern → combine them  \n  Example: <b>Theme A</b> and <b>Theme B</b> have goals that are all <b>In progress</b>\n\n### Formatting Rules\n- Bold ALL themes using <b> tags\n- Bold ALL statuses using <b> tags\n- Allowed statuses ONLY:\n  <b>Not started</b>, <b>In progress</b>, <b>Completed</b>\n- Do NOT paraphrase statuses\n- Do NOT use the word \"category\" or \"categories\".\n\n\n## Language Constraints\n- Do NOT use: \"suggesting\", \"indicating\", \"showcasing\"\n- Do NOT provide interpretation, recommendations, or commentary\n- Do NOT mention effort, performance, or next steps\n- Do NOT include numbers or percentages\n- Do NOT speculate beyond input\n- Output factual statements only\n\n\n## Output Format (STRICT)\n<p><insert goal overview paragraph></p>\n<p><insert progress summary paragraph></p>\n\n\n## Length Constraint\n- TOTAL response MUST be 100 words or less\n\n\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Add node for hcmHrgTeamPerfGoalCreation case branch",
            "name": "Add (hcmHrgTeamPerfGoalCreation Case)"
